{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV","text":"KComponents"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Level 1 is the connected components with an edge and level 2 the blocks of three or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices. Each higher level refines each component of the level below: vertices of fewer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than k neighbors are peeled off, and each piece left is either k-connected or split by a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex cut X of fewer than k vertices into parts D, each searched again as D ∪ X. A cut is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"found by Even’s method, unit-capacity flows on the split network between each of k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices and every later one it is not adjacent to, each stopped after k augmenting paths.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n + m) for levels 1 and 2; each refinement at level k makes at most k n","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flows of O(k (n + m)) each.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity","style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"name":"Connectivity","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","title":"kComponents()","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P12ConnectivityE11kComponentsAD11KComponentsVyxGyF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","remoteSource":{"fileName":"KComponents.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/KComponents.swift#L80"}},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kcomponents()"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components for every k (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k, the maximal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sets of vertices whose induced subgraph has more than k vertices and no vertex cut of fewer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices. Parallel edges count once and self-loops not at all."}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kComponents()"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph/kComponents()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kComponents()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components for every k (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k, the maximal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sets of vertices whose induced subgraph has more than k vertices and no vertex cut of fewer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices. Parallel edges count once and self-loops not at all."}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kcomponents()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KComponents","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity11KComponentsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"kComponents()"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity","abstract":[],"title":"Connectivity"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","title":"Graph","abstract":[],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/KComponents":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents","title":"KComponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}]}}}